// Loop uses the sora-creator-suite FACTORY prompts (a hyper-symmetric packing-line scene), NOT
// Extend Clip's sell-script. Fixed image + video prompts with a single [PRODUCT_NAME] slot
// (substituted server-side) and NO LLM. The image is the shared base frame; every clip animates
// it with the same factory video prompt; audio is ambient-only (silent). The editor schema is
// still cloned from Extend so the operator can edit Loop's own image/video prompts. The
// per-product color/mood comes from the product reference image. [[flow-loop-mode]]
(function setFlowLoopFactoryPrompts() {
  const FACTORY_IMAGE = `⚠️ CRITICAL UNIFORM RULE — LOCKED, NO EXCEPTIONS ⚠️
ALL factory workers MUST wear 100% PURE WHITE uniforms ONLY. Pure white polo/shirt, pure white hairnet, pure white face mask, pure white gloves. ABSOLUTELY NO blue, NO navy, NO black, NO grey, NO pink, NO colored shirt, NO colored uniform of any kind. The uniform color is HARD-LOCKED to pure white in every single output, no matter what product is shown.

Highly polished, hyper-symmetric commercial photograph set inside a vast modern product packing factory. A long stainless steel conveyor line runs DEAD CENTER through the frame from foreground to a deep vanishing point in the distance — perfectly symmetrical composition with everything mirrored on both sides. Many identical units of [PRODUCT_NAME] are lined up neatly along the belt, each individually wrapped in clear transparent protective plastic so the product's shape stays clearly recognizable. Female factory workers in PURE WHITE uniforms (white polo shirts, white hairnets, white face masks, white gloves — NEVER blue, NEVER navy, NEVER colored) work along BOTH sides of the line — symmetrically positioned, mirrored postures, calm focused expressions. Stacks of branded cardboard boxes (in colors that complement the product's palette) are arranged on both sides as decorative walls of inventory. The atmosphere is glossy, aspirational, almost cinematic — bright crisp lighting with subtle highlights, premium e-commerce vibe.

IMPORTANT — adapt ONLY the following to THIS SPECIFIC PRODUCT: box color, accent lighting, and overall color grading pulled from the product's own palette (e.g. pink product → pink-themed boxes and pastel accents). DO NOT adapt the uniform color — uniforms stay PURE WHITE regardless of product. Different products must look clearly distinct driven by their box color / lighting / palette ONLY. For the SAME product keep camera angle, framing, lighting and color tone CONSISTENT and STABLE across shots, so multiple clips of one product concatenate into a smooth non-jarring loop.

SYMMETRY IS CRITICAL: center the conveyor, mirror the workers, mirror the box stacks, vanishing point dead center.

NEGATIVE — must NOT appear under any circumstance: blue uniform, navy uniform, dark blue shirt, black uniform, grey uniform, colored polo, casual outfit, street clothes, lab coat, surgical scrubs, colorful workwear, tinted uniform, text, captions, logos, on-screen graphics, numbers, price tags.

FINAL REMINDER (most important): Workers wear PURE WHITE uniforms ONLY. Pure white shirt. Pure white. Not blue. Not navy. Not any other color. Pure white only — every worker, every shot, every product.`;

  const FACTORY_VIDEO = `⚠️ CRITICAL UNIFORM RULE — LOCKED, NO EXCEPTIONS ⚠️
ALL factory workers MUST wear 100% PURE WHITE uniforms ONLY throughout the ENTIRE video, every single frame. Pure white polo/shirt, pure white hairnet, pure white face mask, pure white gloves. ABSOLUTELY NO blue, NO navy, NO black, NO grey, NO pink, NO colored shirt, NO colored uniform of any kind. The uniform color is HARD-LOCKED to pure white — never changes mid-video, never drifts, never morphs into another color.

⚠️ CONSISTENCY LOCK — NO MID-VIDEO DRIFT ⚠️
The scene, characters, uniform color, lighting, camera angle, and overall composition MUST stay 100% identical from frame 1 to the final frame. Do NOT change uniform color mid-video. Do NOT swap characters. Do NOT shift the scene. Do NOT alter the factory setting. The video must look like a single continuous shot with zero scene changes, zero outfit changes, zero environment changes.

Highly polished, hyper-symmetric commercial video of a vast modern product packing factory. A long stainless steel conveyor line runs DEAD CENTER from foreground to a deep vanishing point in the distance — perfectly symmetrical composition. Many identical units of [PRODUCT_NAME] move slowly along the belt, each unit individually wrapped in clear transparent protective plastic so the product's shape stays clearly recognizable. Female factory workers in PURE WHITE uniforms (white polo shirts, white hairnets, white face masks, white gloves — NEVER blue, NEVER navy, NEVER colored) work along BOTH sides of the line — symmetrically positioned, mirrored postures, calm focused movements as they pick up and pack each unit. Stacks of branded cardboard boxes in colors complementing the product's palette line both sides as decorative walls of inventory. Bright cinematic lighting, glossy aspirational atmosphere, premium e-commerce factory vibe. Steady locked camera holding the symmetric composition, calm continuous workflow.

AUDIO — STRICT: ONLY ambient factory machinery sounds (conveyor belt hum, gentle mechanical clicks, distant warehouse noise). ABSOLUTELY NO background music, NO BGM, NO melody, NO song, NO instrumental music, NO soundtrack, NO musical score of any kind. NO spoken dialogue, NO narration, NO voiceover. NO on-screen text, no captions, no subtitles, no logos.

NEGATIVE — must NOT appear in ANY frame: blue uniform, navy uniform, dark blue shirt, black uniform, grey uniform, colored polo, casual outfit, street clothes, lab coat, surgical scrubs, colorful workwear, tinted uniform, scene change, outfit change mid-video, character morph, environment shift, camera cut, text, captions, logos, subtitles, numbers, price tags.

AUDIO NEGATIVE — must NOT be in the audio track: background music, BGM, melody, song, instrumental music, soundtrack, musical score, piano, guitar, drums, beat, rhythm, electronic music, ambient music, cinematic music, lo-fi music, spoken dialogue, narration, voiceover.

FINAL REMINDER (most important): Workers wear PURE WHITE uniforms ONLY in EVERY frame from start to end. Pure white shirt. Pure white. Not blue. Not navy. Not any other color. Scene stays identical throughout — no mid-video changes of any kind.`;

  // Loop has no LLM script, but submitJob still reads primaryKey (contentSystemPrompt) and bails
  // if it's empty (the +เพิ่มลงคิว button would silently do nothing), so give it a short note —
  // the REAL image/video prompts come from imagePromptTemplate/videoPromptTemplate below and the
  // image prompt overrides this at submit. contentPrompt falls back to this note but _think_loop
  // ignores it (no LLM). The factory prompt is no-text by design → NoText variants are equal.
  const defaults = {
    contentSystemPrompt: "โหมด Loop: คลิปฉากโรงงานแพ็กสินค้า สร้างอัตโนมัติ ไม่มีบทพูด (แก้ Prompt ภาพ/วิดีโอด้านล่าง)",
    contentSystemPromptExtended: "",
    imagePromptTemplate: FACTORY_IMAGE,
    imagePromptTemplateNoText: FACTORY_IMAGE,
    videoPromptTemplate: FACTORY_VIDEO,
    videoPromptTemplateNoText: FACTORY_VIDEO,
  };
  for (let k = 2; k <= 9; k++) {
    defaults[`videoPrompt${k}Template`] = FACTORY_VIDEO;
    defaults[`videoPrompt${k}TemplateNoText`] = FACTORY_VIDEO;
  }
  if (window.PROMPT_DEFAULTS) window.PROMPT_DEFAULTS["flow-loop"] = defaults;
  if (window.PROMPT_SCHEMA && window.PROMPT_SCHEMA["flow-extend"]) {
    window.PROMPT_SCHEMA["flow-loop"] = Object.assign(
      JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(window.PROMPT_SCHEMA["flow-extend"])),
      { title: "Google Flow · Loop" }
    );
  }
})();
